{"id": "11th_tamil_u4_q086", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_4", "lesson_id": "poem_tholkappiya_paayiram", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "boundary_of_tamil_land", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "‘வடவேங்கடம் தென்குமரி ஆயிடைத் / தமிழ்கூறும் நல்லுலகத்து...’ - பனம்பாரனார் குறிப்பிடும் தமிழ்நாட்டின் வடக்கு மற்றும் தெற்கு எல்லைகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "இமயமலை; இலங்கை", "B": "வடக்கில் வேங்கட மலை (திருப்பதி); தெற்கில் குமரி முனை", "C": "விந்திய மலை; காவிரி", "D": "கோதாவரி; வைகை"}, "explanation": "பண்டைய தமிழ்நாட்டின் வட எல்லை வேங்கட மலையாகவும் (திருப்பதி), தென் எல்லை குமரி முனையாகவும் விளங்கியதை இப்பாயிரம் அறுதியிட்டுக் கூறுகிறது."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "According to the famous verse 'Vadavengadam Thenkumari aayidaith...', what were the northern and southern geographic borders of ancient Tamil land?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Himalayas in north; Sri Lanka in south", "B": "Mount Vengadam (Tirupati) in the north; Cape Kumari in the south", "C": "Vindhyas in north; Kaveri in south", "D": "Godavari in north; Vaigai in south"}, "explanation": "Mount Vengadam in the north and Cape Kumari in the south demarcated the linguistic borders of ancient Tamilagam."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book